title The walk a meter could not open
prompt Approved judgment to kg, molting or breaching docs where necessary, following the fascia connections home to root and down to leaves.
think I LOOKED FOR DRIFT MY OWN DAY HAD CAUSED AND FOUND THE FASCIA SOUND. Living docs naming the roster's cost are all testimony -- stamped basenames and an append-only ledger -- so accrete-never-break holds them. docs-geode/README.md's stale page count was repaired on 20260910 and now names its number as history. And the Rishi references teach 25 of the 26 verbs the language declares, so my not knowing read-file existed was mine rather than the docs'.
think So I measured the fascia instead of guessing, with the tree's own lint, and duty 3 reported 24 orphan roster pages. SPLITTING THEM BY WHETHER MAP.md REACHES EACH is what turned one finding into two: seven were already reachable and the meter called them orphans anyway, and seventeen were reachable from nowhere at all.
think MAP.md is the right home rather than docs/README, and read-scope says why in its own words -- the walk that replaces the root ls. A front door absent from it is absent from the one page a lap is told to navigate by.
obs THE PREDICTION WAS WRITTEN IN THE CLAIM AND IT WAS WRONG IN AN INFORMATIVE DIRECTION. I said the lint's count would fall by at most seven; it fell by ZERO. Which rooms I linked was irrelevant to a meter whose inbound set cannot open the page they were linked from. That is a sharper confirmation than the fall I expected would have been: the reading never moves when the fault is repaired, so nothing tells a hand the repair worked.
obs linengrow was the sharpest of the seventeen -- named in the module-ring table in bare backticks where every sibling row carried a link, so a reader's eye passes over a room the table means to offer. Four more wore the same shape: construction, session-logs, active-reviving and counsel.
obs Unreachable fell 17 to 0, MAP.md's 73 cited paths all resolve, and its card reads B+ at 88 which stands. The meter still reads 24, honestly, and the row says so.
loom orphans_reported=24 false_orphans=7 unreachable_before=17 unreachable_after=0
loom lint_duty3_before=24 lint_duty3_after=24 predicted_fall_max=7 actual_fall=0
loom map_cited_paths=73 unresolved=0 map_qa=88 ledger_headroom=4472
rota none -- an approved fascia pass
file MAP.md thirteen module rooms, two workroom front doors and one reading-room shelf gain links; linengrow's bare backticks become a link like every sibling
file construction/REDS.md books %823 -- a reachability meter measuring its own roster rather than the tree's fascia
scope one page repaired, one row booked, the meter left to its lane
status sent -- both remotes
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- widening the lint's inbound set to include MAP.md belongs to the lane that owns it, and the 24 it still reports is a number about a roster until someone does.
